review_text:
I lost my girlfriend;
I have not spoken with anyone for 1 year;
I failed the during last year mature exam;
It ruined my life;
And I'm still fighting with my family because of this game. But np. Everything is ok. Because I'm happy with this game.

I hated every second of playing this game. 

p.s. we will always miss you Jovita ;--; 

twitch. tv/ ezrathemachine

So...Lucius... :[
I would say the idea behind the story is alright, the kills are different (in a good way) and the graphics are pretty decent, especially that this game came out 12 years ago but... it has its big lows:

-Sometimes I felt like the writing was a little cringe (imo);
-Some kills felt really vague in terms of understanding how to do them;
-As other people mentioned in the discussion section of this game it can have some performance issues (for example my game kept crashing at the end of chapter 4. Good thing I had an ace on my sleeve ;)
-The "smart-ahh"/puzzle ending was really stupid with McGuffin and Lucius walking out from the manor lie two bad-ahhes lol;
- "I like this game" and "I'm addicted" achievements shouldn't even exist since this game is 2-3 hours long;
-AND the voice acting..."sigh"... At the beginning it wasn't noticeable, it felt normal, but through the last half of the game... it could have been much better.
  And just the fact that I heard the other two instalments got even worse than this one pains me, since my pros still stand out. If only this game and the other two from the trilogy got a whole remake (too late for that sadly), I would gladly come to play this one again.
But for now 5-7/10.

First of all I can't really understand why this game has mostly positive reviews. Death ideas are clichéd. The plot is non-existent. Shooting someone with a pistol, or using a fireball results in a hit-and-run like effect on the victim. Hitman 2 required a full clip to be emptied on a victim to get this effect. Lucius' cannon would flabbergast even Dirty Harry. The fire extinguisher scene from the end of the game should occur in the game studio during the production phase. The 20h and 40h achievements are an offence in their own right. Especially that the playthrough takes 10 hours if you take a nap in the meantime. It's good that you can sleep through their completion.  

   - 'Unique 3D horror adventure gaming experience'  - depends on one's definition of 'unique';
   - '3D Open World' - to some extent;
   - 'Cinematic Cut-scenes' - but surely not climatic;
   - 'Breathtaking Atmosphere and Stunning Visuals' - breathtaking like a cockroach on a kitchen table;
   - 'Harness Supernatural Powers, including Telekinesis and Mind Control' - if you can harness the game physics to move items;
  - 'Experience the terror of a classic tale from the horror movie genre' - terror indeed.

Shiver Games breaks the fourth wall by making the player scared with how the game is made, not by the game itself. Cheers to that!
